Notebook[{
Cell["Key Equations for the Dynamic Active-Strain Beam Formulation", "Title", FontFamily->"Arial", FontSize->40, FontWeight->"Plain", FontColor->RGBColor[0.85,0.04,0.02], CellMargins->{{18,24},{18,24}}],

Cell["This supplementary notebook collects the key mathematical expressions used in the dynamic beam reduction and analytical inverse reconstruction. The equations are arranged in the order of the formulation: through-thickness recurrence relations, dimensional beam balances and averaged stress, nondimensional and integrated equations, the axial-stretch and rotation representation, and the two inverse active-stretch coefficients. Each block is preceded by a short description of its role and notation.", "Text", FontFamily->"Times New Roman", FontSize->14, LineSpacing->{1.2,0}, CellMargins->{{54,24},{8,10}}],

Cell["Notation: X, Z and t are the dimensional reference coordinates and time; S and \:03c4 are the nondimensional longitudinal coordinate and time. x0 and z0 describe the bottom-surface position, while x1, z1 and the higher-index functions are position coefficients in the thickness expansion; p0 and its higher-index counterparts are pressure coefficients. Nx0 and Nz0 denote the nondimensional bottom-surface coordinates. N\:03bb10 and N\:03bb11 are the nondimensional zeroth and first through-thickness coefficients of longitudinal active stretch. f and g denote the bottom-surface stretch and tangent angle. Df is the relative axial-stretch correction in the forward reduction. h0 is the nondimensional half-thickness, and \:03b5 is the inertia parameter. Component labels 1 and 3 follow the original x\:2013z notation used in the equations.", "Text", FontFamily->"Times New Roman", FontSize->14, LineSpacing->{1.2,0}, CellMargins->{{54,24},{8,10}}],

Cell["1. Through-thickness recurrence relations", "Section", FontFamily->"Arial", FontSize->24, FontWeight->"Plain", FontColor->RGBColor[0.85,0.24,0.03], CellFrame->{{0,0},{0,0.5}}, CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.72], CellMargins->{{18,24},{10,24}}, CellFrameMargins->{{0,0},{0,10}}],

Cell["The following expressions give the position and pressure coefficients generated by the through-thickness recurrence. They retain the dimensional variables and the original load, material and inertial terms. The coefficients connect the bottom-surface fields to the higher-order terms used in the reduced balances.", "Text", FontFamily->"Times New Roman", FontSize->14, LineSpacing->{1.2,0}, CellMargins->{{54,24},{8,10}}],

